BuildOptions
	Controls how resource modifications are applied
	when the Apply button is clicked.
	
	Rebuild on every resource change
		New instances of each object implied in the
		resource change are created for each resource 
		modification. In this mode, the effect of
		changes is immediately visible, for all resources.
		This is the default mode. It is slower than the
		others, but easier to use.
	
	SetValues on every resource change
		Resource values are updated on existing objects.
		Though most resource changes are directly visible,
		some changes, for some widgets, are not. Some resources
		cannot be changed by SetValues and for these,
		an error message is generated which may be ignored.
		In addition, it is not possible to observe the return
		of resources to their default values when changes are
		removed. All changes become effective when the Apply
		button is clicked in the Resources Box.
		This mode is faster than the default mode but can
		prove misleading for inexperienced users.
	
	Rebuild on resources window Apply
		None of the widget's resources are updated until
		the Apply button is clicked in the Resources Box.
		In this mode, none of the changes can be observed
		immediately, but there is a significant gain in
		speed of operation.
		Meant for experienced users, this is the fastest
		of the three modes.
		